========================================
Root Cause
========================================
Kernel logic error in grid/block mapping or WMMA fragment usage.
The tensor core MMA operations either:
- Execute on wrong data (indexing bug)
- Accumulate incorrectly across K-tiles
- Store to wrong output locations
- Fragment layout mismatch (row/col major confusion)

Multiple grid/block rewrites attempted; none passed correctness.
WMMA fragment API for m16n16k16 FP16 is functional (compiles) but
the surrounding kernel structure has unverified bugs.

========================================
Attempts Made
========================================
1. Initial: block=(128,4), warp_id=ty (wrong: 128 threads = 4 warps per ty)
2. Rewrite: block=(32,8), warp_row/col mapping, 8 warps/block
3. Grid calculations revised multiple times

All variants compiled and ran but failed correctness with massive errors.
No variant produced numerically valid output.

========================================
Conclusion
========================================
FP16 Tensor Core baseline NOT ESTABLISHED.
Correctness gate is a hard requirement — this experiment fails it.

The WMMA API for FP16 m16n16k16 is available in CUDA 13.3 but
writing a correct, complete GEMM kernel around it requires more
iterations than this cycle allows.

Next step options:
A. Debug kernel with SASS/PTX inspection (time-consuming)
B. Switch to CUTLASS reference implementation (external dependency)
C. Return to FP32 CUDA-core and explore async/TMA path

RECOMMENDATION: Option C — the accepted FP32 kernel (0.265 ms) is
stable and verified. The async/TMA path on Blackwell is the
architectural successor for this codebase.

